===Etymology 1===
[[File:First amendment engraving, Washington DC.jpg|thumb|upright=0.9|The [[First Amendment]] to the {{w|United States Constitution}} [[engrave]]d on the [[facade]] of the {{w|Newseum}} in [[Washington, D.C.]] In part, it reads: "Congress shall make no law {{...}} abridging {{...}} the right of the people peaceably to assemble, and to petition the government for a redress of grievances."]]

From {{inh|en|enm|redressen}}, from {{der|en|xno|radresser}}, {{m|nrf|redrescer}}, {{m|nrf|redrescier}} and {{der|en|frm|redresser||to [[stand#Verb|stand]] (someone or something) up; to [[stand up]] again; to [[rebuild]], to [[repair]] something [[damaged]], to [[rectify]], to [[restore]]; to [[obtain]] redress; to [[cure#Verb|cure]]; (of hair) to stand on end; to [[revise]] a [[judgment]]}} (modern {{cog|fr|redresser}}), from {{der|en|fro|redrecier||to stand (someone or something) up; to stand up again}}, from {{der|en|fro|re-||[[again]], [[once more]]}} (from {{der|en|la|re-}}, from {{der|en|itc-pro|*wre-|t=again}}; further etymology uncertain) + {{der|en|fro|drechier}}, {{m|fro|drecier}}, {{m|fro|dresser||to [[dress#Verb|dress]]; to stand up}} (from {{der|en|la-vul|*drēctiāre}}, a contracted form of {{m|la|*dīrēctiāre}}, from {{der|en|la|dīrēctus||[[straight]]}}).

Compare {{cog|ca|redreçar}}, {{cog|es|redreçar}} {{qualifier|obsolete}}, {{cog|it|redreçare}}, {{m|it|redrezare}}, {{m|it|redricciare}}, {{m|it|ridirizzare}} {{qualifier|all obsolete}}, {{m|it|ridrizzare}}, {{cog|la-lat|redressare||to [[repair]]; to [[set#Verb|set]] [[right]]}}, {{cog|pro|redreisar}}, {{m|pro|redresar}}.

