# To [[dress]] again.
#* {{quote-book|en|author=W[illiam] Brian Rowe|chapter=Grinding Wheel Dressing|title=Principles of Modern Grinding Technology|location=Oxford; Burlington, Mass.|publisher=William Andrew, {{w|Elsevier}}|year=2009|pages=71–72|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=iyvMUa7PwcUC&pg=PA72|isbn=978-0-8155-2018-4|passage=The position of the grinding wheel surface relative to the machine axis positions continually changes due to grinding wheel wear, thermal expansion of the machine tool, and thermal expansion or contraction of the grinding wheel. {{...}} The effect of this variability is that the wheel position stored in the CNC &#91;[[w:Numerical control|computer numerical control]]&#93; is inaccurate by the time it is necessary to '''re-dress''' the grinding wheel. To overcome this problem, the machine user often specifies a large dressing in-feed to guarantee that the dressing tool will dress the grinding wheel.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2009|author=John C. Barber|title=The Joy of Medical Practice: Forty Years of Interesting Patients|page=22
|passage=I talked with her mother whenever she was in the room while I '''redressed''' the wound.}}
# {{lb|en|film}} To [[redecorate]] a previously [[existing]] [[film set]] so that it can [[double#Verb|double]] for another set.
#* {{quote-book|en|author=Michael P. DiPaolo|chapter=How to be a Guerrilla Filmmaker|title=The Six Day Horror Movie: A No-Nonsense Guide to No-Budget Filmmaking|location=Jefferson, N.C.|publisher=w:McFarland & Company|year=2004|page=120|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=1Ml-VlcNGh0C&pg=PA120|isbn=978-0-7864-1905-0|passage=[[w:Val Lewton|[Val] Lewton]] would '''redress''' standing sets, turning a church into an insane asylum or the staircase for {{w|Orson Welles}}' ''[[w:The Magnificent Ambersons (film)|The Magnificent Ambersons]]'' into the staircase for the young girl's apartment in ''[[w:Cat People (1942 film)|Cat People]]''. {{...}} [Y]ou should be thinking about trying to reuse every location you have as another location, either by using another room or another angle or '''re-dressing''' what's already there.}}

